## 4.1 Deque

A deque is a collection that can perform both stack-like (LIFO - last in first out) and queue-like (FIFO - first in first out) operations.

The most common operations you will use on a deque are the insertion and removal of elements. In a stack (LIFO), you can only remove an element (pop) from the top of the stack, and insert elements (push) only at the top. In a queue (FIFO), you cannot remove elements from the top. Instead, only elements can be pushed at the rear (right end), and removed from the front (left end).

In this exercise, you will implement a deque.

