## 1.2 - XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)

XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) is an attack where a web page steals some cookies and uses them to inject javascript code 
into an unsuspecting user. The attacker creates a link that will direct the user to a malicious website. Once the user 
is directed to the malicious website, the attacker will try to steal the cookies from the user.

XSS vulnerabilities allow an attacker to execute arbitrary scripts inside a victim's browser, allowing the attacker to
steal cookies and then use those cookies to attack other websites and access user accounts.

