The solution is to split the template into two parts:

* The parts that you want to be inserted, such as the method
* The remaining parts that you want to generate, such as a function to sanitize the file name

This can be done by using the following template syntax:

```
<|insert method here|>
<|insert function here|>

```

Then the function `insert_method()` and `insert_function()` are used to insert the parts into the main template. For example:

```
$template = file_get_contents("./template.txt");
$template = insert_method($template);
$template = insert_function($template);

function insert_method($text) {
    $method = file_get_contents("./method.txt");
    $match = "/<|insert method here|>/";
    $method = preg_replace($match, $method, $text);
    return $method;
}

function insert_function($text) {
    $function = file_get_contents("./function.txt");
    $match = "/<|insert function here|>/";
    $function = preg_replace($match, $function, $text);
    return $function;
}

