### Java: Finding the index of a substring

**Difficulty**: easy

Given a string and a substring, return the starting index of the substring in the string. If the substring is not present, return -1.

Example:
```java
substring("Java is a programming language", "Java") ➞ 0

substring("JavaScript is a programming language", "Python") ➞ -1

substring("What an easy task, right", "easy") ➞ 14
```

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class ClassX {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Introduce una palabra: ");
        String word = input.next();
        System.out.print("Introduce una substring: ");
        String sub = input.next();

        System.out.println(indexOf(word, sub));
    }

    /**
     * Devuelve -1 si la palabra no esta en el texto
     */
    private static int indexOf(String text, String sub) {
        int i = -1;
        int j = 0;
        int start = 0;
        while (start < text.length() && i == -1) {
            for (i = text.indexOf(sub, start); i >= 0; i = text.indexOf(sub, start)) {
                if (start+1 < i) {
                    break;
                }
                start = i+1;
                j++;
            }
        }
        return j;
    }
}
