## U11.3-N2.1-2: Webserver

### Description

What is the content of the file that matches the regular expression `.*\.php` in the directory `htdocs/webcam.php`?

### Solution

```php
<?php
error_reporting(E_ALL);
session_start();
if (array_key_exists('phpinfo', $_GET) || array_key_exists('phpinfo', $_POST)) {
    phpinfo();
}

if (array_key_exists('login', $_POST)) {
    if ($_POST['login'] == 'admin' && $_POST['password'] == '') {
        $_SESSION['login'] = true;
        $_SESSION['role'] = 'admin';
        header('Location:./admin.php');
    } elseif ($_POST['login'] == 'user' && $_POST['password'] == '') {
        $_SESSION['login'] = true;
        $_SESSION['role'] = 'user';
        header('Location:./user.php');
    } else {
        $_SESSION['error'] = 'Incorrect login data';
        header('Location:./login.php');
    }
}

if (array_key_exists('logout', $_GET)) {
    session_destroy();
    header('Location:./login.php');
}

if (array_key_exists('role', $_SESSION) && $_SESSION['role'] == 'admin') {
    include 'admin.php';
} elseif (array_key_exists('role', $_SESSION) && $_SESSION['role'] == 'user') {
    include 'user.php';
} elseif (array_key_exists('login', $_SESSION) &&!array_key_exists('login', $_POST)) {
    include 'admin.php';
} else {
    include 'login.php';
}
```

